Fix lichess-bot #1184: a transient stream drop abandons a LIVE game.

Upstream: https://github.com/lichess-bot-devs/lichess-bot/issues/1184
Status: closed "not planned", no fix merged.

On any stream exception the handler computes:

    stopped = isinstance(e, StopIteration)
    stay_in_game = not stopped and (move_attempted or game_is_active(li, game.id))

When the stream ends (StopIteration), `not stopped` is False, so short-circuit
evaluation means game_is_active() is NEVER CALLED -- precisely in the case
where we most need to know. The bot leaves the game loop while the game is
still live, the process stays up looking healthy, and it flags on time.

This matters much more on WiFi than on ethernet. On this box the control
stream was observed dropping ~3x per 20 minutes.

game_is_active() already fails safe: if the API is unreachable it returns
True, so the patched version keeps playing rather than abandoning on a
network blip. `stopped` is assigned here and read nowhere else in the file,
so dropping it from the condition has no other effect.

--- a/lib/lichess_bot.py
+++ b/lib/lichess_bot.py
@@
-                    stopped = isinstance(e, StopIteration)
-                    stay_in_game = not stopped and (move_attempted or game_is_active(li, game.id))
+                    # PATCHED (see patches/0001-lichess-bot-1184-stream-drop.patch):
+                    # upstream short-circuits game_is_active() away on
+                    # StopIteration and abandons live games on a network blip.
+                    # Always ask lichess whether the game is really over.
+                    stay_in_game = move_attempted or game_is_active(li, game.id)
